{
  "_comment": [
    "Calibration worksheet for vg360-site (vg360-scenegraph). Fill in on site, then:",
    "  cargo run --release --manifest-path vg360-scenegraph/Cargo.toml --bin vg360-site -- fit config/iogp/worksheet.json --catalog <test1_logpeditor>/iogp-editor/data/vg360_catalog.json -o config/iogp/site.json",
    "Pixels are of the stream tamserve-boxes decodes ([decode] width x height, here 640 x 360), read off a still of it.",
    "Per deck: image_polygon = where that deck is visible; marks = 6-10 points spread over it, {px: [u, v], m: [x, y]} in metres of one deck datum per camera.",
    "With a safety spec on the camera, use that spec's floor metres for m, and copy its K and D into lens (marks are then raw pixels).",
    "Per zone: floor_polygon in metres (from the rig drawings), or image_polygon drawn on the still (mapped through the deck's fit).",
    "Optional height_marks (>= 6, at least two levels 1 m apart: handrail tops, column bands): {px, m: [x, y, z]} -> camera matrix for drop zones under suspended loads.",
    "occluders: image polygons of equipment that hides people's feet."
  ],
